%description:

Tcp.baseMss:other -- the first data segment of the search carries 512 bytes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with mtuProbing: the lower end of the path MTU search ...; an active
opener starts at it, as Linux; at least 88".

The classes: linux (1024, the default, the value of Linux tcp_base_mss), other (another value),
invalid (below 88). The code: TcpConnection::initMtuProbing() checks the value, takes the MTU
of the value as the lower end of the search, and starts an active opener at it. This test separates "other" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with mtuProbing 2 (precondition); host1 sends 1000000 bytes to host2; the path carries 1500 bytes, and the MSS of the handshake
is 1460 (1448 bytes of data with the Timestamps option). A frame carries 52 bytes of IP, TCP and
option headers more than its data: 1500 bytes of IP for 1448 bytes of data. Observation: level 1, the first
data segment carries 512 bytes (564 bytes of IP).

%# parameter: Tcp.baseMss
%# class: other
%# value: 512
%# key: *.host1.tcp.baseMss
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpBaseMssOther")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField == 564B")
             .describe("the first frame of data of host1")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpBaseMssOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.baseMss = 512    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
sim-time-limit = 2s
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 2
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpBaseMssOther: PASS
